{
  "brief_rationale": "The doctor systematically assessed red-flag symptoms, explicitly recognized the severity of ALT 658 U/L after 3 months without repeat testing, elicited missing information, set medication boundaries, formed a concrete next-step plan with cost/transport considerations, obtained patient confirmation and safety-net instructions, and avoided unsupported diagnoses. All eight responsibility chain (RC) items were met with no serious or minor errors. Two case-defined high-order points (HO1: real-world constraint navigation; HO3: safe bounded closure) were actively triggered and completed with meaningful trajectory impact. No important non-chain defect was identified. Closure was safe, executable, and traceable as valid_closure. The model did not trigger HO2 or HO4, preventing grade 5; the completed HO1 and HO3 satisfy the grade 4 threshold.",
